  "final": "I moved the duplicated parsing into one shared module, `dateparse.py`. The 4 existing tests pass with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\n- **Shared module:** `parse_date(value, label)` normalises whitespace and tries the three formats (`%Y-%m-%d`, `%d/%m/%Y`, `%d %b %Y`). If none match, it raises `ValueError(f\"unrecognised {label}: {value!r}\")`.\n- **Wrappers:** `parse_due_date` and `parse_report_date` keep their names and signatures. They are now one-liners that call `parse_date` with \"due date\" or \"report date\". That keeps the two different error messages exactly as they were.\n- **Format constants:** `reports.dates.FORMATS` is still importable, re-exported from the shared module. `schedule.dates._FORMATS` was private and not used anywhere else, so I removed it.\n\n`dateparse.py` sits at the repo root, so it's imported as `from dateparse import ...`. That works when running from the repo root, as the tests do. If you'd rather have it inside a package, tell me which one.",
